=head1 DESCRIPTION

This structure contains information about one Evidently feature in your
account.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 B<REQUIRED> Arn => Str

The ARN of the feature.


=head2 B<REQUIRED> CreatedTime => Str

The date and time that the feature is created.


=head2 DefaultVariation => Str

The name of the variation that is used as the default variation. The
default variation is served to users who are not allocated to any
ongoing launches or experiments of this feature.

This variation must also be listed in the C<variations> structure.

If you omit C<defaultVariation>, the first variation listed in the
C<variations> structure is used as the default variation.


=head2 Description => Str

The description of the feature.


=head2 EntityOverrides => L<Paws::Evidently::EntityOverrideMap>

A set of key-value pairs that specify users who should always be served
a specific variation of a feature. Each key specifies a user using
their user ID, account ID, or some other identifier. The value
specifies the name of the variation that the user is to be served.

For the override to be successful, the value of the key must match the
C<entityId> used in the EvaluateFeature
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudwatchevidently/latest/APIReference/API_EvaluateFeature.html)
operation.


=head2 EvaluationRules => ArrayRef[L<Paws::Evidently::EvaluationRule>]

An array of structures that define the evaluation rules for the
feature.


=head2 B<REQUIRED> EvaluationStrategy => Str

If this value is C<ALL_RULES>, the traffic allocation specified by any
ongoing launches or experiments is being used. If this is
C<DEFAULT_VARIATION>, the default variation is being served to all
users.


=head2 B<REQUIRED> LastUpdatedTime => Str

